## 3. landing-page.css — Deep Dive

This file styles the **product landing page** with a centered hero, spec grid, stat cards, a CTA band, and a scrolling terminal log.

---

### 3.1 Hero — Product Variant (`.hero--product`)

```css
.hero--product { --fs-hero: clamp(5rem, 18vw, 18rem); }
```

The product hero overrides the base hero font size to be slightly smaller than the default. It also adds a decorative circular ring overlaid on the background grid.

```css
.hero--product .hero__grid::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    width: 120px;
    height: 120px;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    border: 1px solid var(--safety);
    border-radius: 50%;
    opacity: 0.15;
}
```

This `::after` pseudo-element creates a faint orange circle centered in the hero — a subtle industrial targeting/crosshair aesthetic.

**Child elements:**

| Class | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `.hero__subtitle` | Uppercase subtitle in `Space Grotesk` bold, muted color |
| `.hero__actions` | Flex row of CTA buttons, centered, wraps on mobile |
| `.hero__coords` | Bottom-left decorative coordinate text (opacity 0.2) |
| `.hero__version` | Bottom-right decorative version text (opacity 0.2) |

---

### 3.2 Product Details Section (`.details__inner`)

Uses a **12-column CSS Grid**. The layout is split:

- Left column (`.details__left`) → spans **5 columns** — text description
- Right column (`.details__right`) → spans **7 columns** — stat cards in a 2-column sub-grid

```css
.details__inner {
    max-width: 1440px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(12, 1fr);
    gap: var(--gap);
    align-items: start;
}
```

**Breakpoints:**
- `≤ 1024px` → Both columns expand to `span 12` (stack vertically)

---

### 3.3 Stat Cards (`.stat-card`)

Stat cards are bordered boxes showing a metric label + large number value.

```css
.stat-card {
    border: var(--border);
    padding: clamp(1.2rem, 2vw, 2rem);
    background: var(--base);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    transition: none;  /* No CSS transition — hover is instant */
}

.stat-card:hover {
    transform: translate(-4px, -4px);
    box-shadow: 12px 12px 0px var(--ink);
}
```

**Hover effect:** The card shifts up-left by 4px and the shadow extends — creates a "lifting" illusion without smooth animation (intentionally mechanical).

**Variants:**

| Class | Background | Shadow color on hover |
|---|---|---|
| `.stat-card` (default) | `--base` (off-white) | `--ink` (black) |
| `.stat-card--dark` | `--ink` (black) | `--safety` (orange) |

**Inner elements:**

| Class | Description |
|---|---|
| `.stat-card__label` | Tiny uppercase label with wide letter-spacing |
| `.stat-card__value` | Large number in `Space Grotesk` bold, tight letter-spacing |
| `.stat-card__unit` | Smaller unit text (e.g., "kg", "°C") — `0.4em` size, semi-transparent |

---

### 3.4 Spec Grid (`.spec-grid`)

A 4-column grid of specification cells with shared borders (no gap — borders overlap).

```css
.spec-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 0;
    border: var(--border);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
}
```

**Border logic for the grid:**
- Every cell has `border-right` and `border-bottom`
- `.spec-cell:nth-child(4n)` → removes right border (last column)
- `.spec-cell:nth-last-child(-n+4)` → removes bottom border (last row)

This creates a seamless joined-border grid without double-borders.

**Breakpoints:**
- `≤ 1024px` → 2 columns
- `≤ 768px` → 1 column (stacked)

**Spec Cell Variants:**

| Class | Background | Text | Hover |
|---|---|---|---|
| Default | `--base` | `--ink` | `--ink` bg, `--base` text |
| `.spec-cell--dark` | `--ink` | `--base` | `--safety` bg |
| `.spec-cell--safety` | `--safety` | `--base` | `--ink` bg |

**Inner elements of `.spec-cell`:**

| Class | Description |
|---|---|
| `.spec-cell__id` | Tiny cell ID (e.g., `SPEC-01`) |
| `.spec-cell__label` | Uppercase metric name |
| `.spec-cell__value` | Large numeric value in `Space Grotesk` |
| `.spec-cell__unit` | Monospace unit string (e.g., `rpm`, `MPa`) |
| `.spec-cell__note` | Small descriptive note at bottom |

---

### 3.5 CTA Band (`.cta-band`)

A centered call-to-action section with title, body text, and buttons.

```css
.cta-band__inner { max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto; }
.cta-band__title { font-size: var(--fs-h1); }
.cta-band__text  { opacity: 0.5; line-height: 1.9; }
.cta-band__actions { display: flex; gap: 1rem; justify-content: center; }
```

---

### 3.6 Terminal Log (`.log`)

A horizontally scrolling ticker that mimics a terminal output stream.

```css
.log { background: var(--term-bg); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--safety); }
```

**How the animation works:**

```css
.log__track {
    display: flex;
    width: max-content;
    animation: tickerScroll 40s linear infinite;
}
.log__track--reverse {
    animation-direction: reverse;
    animation-duration: 55s;
}
```

Two tracks scroll in opposite directions at different speeds, creating a layered live-feed effect.

**The mask fade:**
```css
.log__body {
    mask-image: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent 0%, black 4%, black 96%, transparent 100%);
}
```

This fades out the left and right edges of the ticker so entries appear to scroll in from the side naturally.

**Log entry types (color coding):**

| Class | Color | Border | Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `.log-ok` | `--term-green` | Green tint | OK / success |
| `.log-warn` | `--term-amber` | Amber tint | Warning |
| `.log-sys` | `--safety` | Orange tint | System message |

