## 5. the-observer.css — Deep Dive

The most complex page — a **two-panel shell** with a main content area and a fixed terminal sidebar. It includes a radar-sweep hero, a metrics ribbon, a features grid, and a signal visualizer.

---

### 5.1 Shell Layout (`.shell`)

```css
.shell {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr var(--sidebar-w, 340px);
    min-height: 100vh;
}
```

The outer page wrapper is a 2-column grid. The sidebar is a fixed 340px wide. At `≤ 1024px`, this collapses to 1 column and the sidebar becomes a hidden off-canvas panel.

---

### 5.2 Radar Hero (`.hero--radar`)

```css
.hero--radar { --fs-hero: clamp(3.5rem, 10vw, 10rem); }
```

Smaller hero font size than other variants (data/dashboard feel, not marketing).

**Decorative radar rings:**

```css
.hero__ring:nth-child(1) { width: 200px;  height: 200px; }
.hero__ring:nth-child(2) { width: 400px;  height: 400px; }
.hero__ring:nth-child(3) { width: 650px;  height: 650px; }
.hero__ring:nth-child(4) { width: 950px;  height: 950px; }
```

Four concentric circles centered around a point (45% from left, 30% from top) — gives an off-center radar / sonar look.

**The sweeping arm animation:**
```css
.hero__ring:nth-child(1)::after {
    content: '';
    width: 475px;
    height: 1px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--safety), transparent);
    transform-origin: 0 0;
    animation: sweepArm 8s linear infinite;
}

@keyframes sweepArm {
    from { transform: rotate(0deg); }
    to   { transform: rotate(360deg); }
}
```

A horizontal line (gradient from orange to transparent) rotates 360° continuously from its left end — mimicking a radar sweep.

---

### 5.3 Metrics Ribbon (`.ribbon`)

A horizontal 5-column strip of quick metrics below the hero.

```css
.ribbon {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
    border-bottom: var(--border);
}
```

**Notable cell behavior:**
- Cell 3 (`.ribbon__cell:nth-child(3)`) is dark by default — a visual highlight in the middle of the ribbon
- On hover → cells invert to `--ink` background with white text
- Cell 3 on hover → changes to `--safety` orange

**Breakpoints:**
- `≤ 1024px` → 3 columns
- `≤ 768px` → 2 columns
- `≤ 480px` → 1 column

---

### 5.4 Features Grid (`.features__grid`)

A 3-column grid of feature cards with joined borders (same pattern as the spec grid in landing page).

```css
.features__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 0;
    border: var(--border);
}
```

**Border removal rules:**
- `nth-child(3n)` → no right border (last in each row)
- `nth-last-child(-n+3)` → no bottom border (last row)

**Feature Card Variants:**

| Class | BG | Text | Hover |
|---|---|---|---|
| Default | `--base` | `--ink` | `--ink` bg |
| `.feat-card--dark` | `--ink` | `--base` | `--safety` bg |
| `.feat-card--safety` | `--safety` | `--base` | `--ink` bg |

**Spark bars in feature cards:**
```css
.feat-card .spark__bar          { background: var(--safety); }
.feat-card--dark .spark__bar    { background: var(--term-green); }
.feat-card--safety .spark__bar  { background: var(--base); }
.feat-card:hover .spark__bar    { background: var(--safety); }
```

Spark bars change color depending on which card variant they're inside — and change again on hover.

---

### 5.5 Signal Visualizer (`.signal__viz`)

A live animated bar chart inside a dark panel — simulates a signal or frequency visualization.

```css
.signal__viz {
    border: var(--border);
    background: var(--ink);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--base);
}
```

**Animation:**
```css
.signal__viz-bar {
    flex: 1;
    background: var(--term-green);
    opacity: 0.6;
    animation: waveBar 1.5s ease-in-out infinite alternate;
}

.signal__viz-bar:nth-child(3n) { background: var(--safety); }
.signal__viz-bar:nth-child(7n) { background: var(--term-amber); }

@keyframes waveBar {
    0%   { height: 15%; }
    25%  { height: 65%; }
    50%  { height: 30%; }
    75%  { height: 80%; }
    100% { height: 20%; }
}
```

Each bar animates height between keyframes. Odd bars, 3n bars, and 7n bars have `animation-delay` offsets so bars don't all move in sync — creates an organic wave pattern. Every 3rd bar is orange, every 7th is amber, rest are green.

---

### 5.6 Terminal Sidebar (`.sidebar`)

A fixed-position dark panel on the right side — the most complex single component in the template.

```css
.sidebar {
    position: fixed;
    top: var(--header-h);
    right: 0;
    width: var(--sidebar-w, 340px);
    height: calc(100vh - var(--header-h));
    background: var(--term-bg);
    border-left: var(--border);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    z-index: 900;
    overflow: hidden;
}
```

**Sidebar sections (top to bottom):**

1. **Header** (`.sidebar__header`) — Title with pulsing green dot + metadata
2. **Stats row** (`.sidebar__stats`) — 3-column mini stats grid
3. **Mini chart** (`.sidebar__chart`) — Bar chart with green/orange columns
4. **Log scroll** (`.sidebar__log`) — Auto-scrolling terminal log
5. **Footer** (`.sidebar__footer`) — Tiny metadata row

**The auto-scrolling log:**
```css
.sidebar__log-track {
    animation: logScrollV 60s linear infinite;
}

@keyframes logScrollV {
    0%   { transform: translateY(0); }
    100% { transform: translateY(-50%); }
}
```

The log duplicates its content (2× height), then scrolls by exactly `-50%` — creating seamless infinite vertical scrolling.

**Fade masks on log:**
```css
.sidebar__log::before { top: 0;    background: linear-gradient(var(--term-bg), transparent); }
.sidebar__log::after  { bottom: 0; background: linear-gradient(transparent, var(--term-bg)); }
```

Top and bottom edges fade out — entries appear to emerge from and disappear into the terminal.

**Mobile toggle:**
```css
.sidebar-toggle {
    display: none;
    position: fixed;
    bottom: 1rem;
    right: 1rem;
    z-index: 1100;
    width: 48px;
    height: 48px;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--term-green);
    border: 2px solid var(--safety);
}
```

At `≤ 1024px`, the sidebar is hidden and a toggle button appears in the bottom-right corner. Clicking it adds/removes the `.open` class.

