## 8. Dark Mode Implementation Guide

> ⚠️ **This template has NO built-in dark mode.** Every color is hardcoded — `--base` is always off-white, `--ink` is always near-black. There is no `prefers-color-scheme` or dark class variant anywhere.

Here is a **complete dark mode system** you can add to your project.

---

### 8.1 Understanding What Needs to Flip

The template uses a light-on-dark/dark-on-light duality already — many components have a `--dark` variant with inverted colors. Dark mode is essentially **making the page default look like those `--dark` variants**.

**Colors that need to flip:**

| Variable | Light Mode | Dark Mode |
|---|---|---|
| `--base` | `#F5F5F0` (off-white) | `#0A0A08` (near-black) |
| `--ink` | `#0A0A08` (near-black) | `#F5F5F0` (off-white) |
| `--surface` | `#EDEDEA` | `#141412` |
| `--muted` | `#888` | `#666` |
| `--safety` | `#FF3E00` ← **stays the same** | `#FF3E00` |
| `--term-bg` | `#0D0D0B` ← **stays the same** | `#0D0D0B` |
| `--shadow` | `8px 8px 0 #0A0A08` | `8px 8px 0 rgba(245,245,240,0.15)` |
| `--shadow-safety` | `8px 8px 0 #FF3E00` ← **stays the same** | `8px 8px 0 #FF3E00` |
| `--border` | `1px solid #0A0A08` | `1px solid rgba(245,245,240,0.15)` |
| `--border-thin` | `1px solid rgba(10,10,8,0.12)` | `1px solid rgba(245,245,240,0.08)` |

---

### 8.2 Recommended Implementation — CSS Class Toggle

**Step 1:** Add this to your base CSS (in `templatemo-axis-industrial.css` or a new file):

```css
/* === DARK MODE OVERRIDES === */
/* Add class="dark" to <html> or <body> to activate */

html.dark {
    --base:        #0A0A08;
    --ink:         #F5F5F0;
    --surface:     #141412;
    --muted:       #666666;
    --border:      1px solid rgba(245, 245, 240, 0.15);
    --border-thin: 1px solid rgba(245, 245, 240, 0.08);
    --shadow:      8px 8px 0px rgba(245, 245, 240, 0.12);
}
```

The `--safety`, `--term-bg`, `--term-green`, and `--term-amber` stay the same — they already work on dark backgrounds.

**Step 2:** Override components that hardcode colors directly:

```css
/* Stat cards with hardcoded backgrounds */
html.dark .stat-card {
    background: #1A1A18;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
}

html.dark .stat-card--dark {
    background: #F5F5F0;
    color: #0A0A08;
}

/* Stack cards with hardcoded backgrounds */
html.dark .stack__card:nth-child(2) { background: #1C1C1A; }
html.dark .stack__card:nth-child(4) { background: #181816; }

/* Surface sections */
html.dark .about { background: #111110; }

/* Bento visual circles — currentColor will now be light */
/* No override needed — currentColor adapts automatically */
```

**Step 3:** Add a toggle button and JavaScript:

```html
<!-- Add this button in your nav or header -->
<button id="dark-toggle" aria-label="Toggle dark mode">
    <span id="theme-icon">☀</span>
</button>
```

```javascript
// Dark mode toggle logic
const html = document.documentElement;
const toggle = document.getElementById('dark-toggle');
const icon = document.getElementById('theme-icon');

// On load — restore saved preference
const savedTheme = localStorage.getItem('theme');
if (savedTheme === 'dark' || (!savedTheme && window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches)) {
    html.classList.add('dark');
    icon.textContent = '☽';
}

// Toggle on click
toggle.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const isDark = html.classList.toggle('dark');
    icon.textContent = isDark ? '☽' : '☀';
    localStorage.setItem('theme', isDark ? 'dark' : 'light');
});
```

