### 8.4 Dark Mode Styling Notes Per Component

**Terminal Sidebar & Log** — Already dark by default (`var(--term-bg)` = `#0D0D0B`). In dark mode, the sidebar will still look correct. You may want to darken its border:

```css
html.dark .sidebar { border-left-color: rgba(245,245,240,0.08); }
```

**Hero Grid Lines** — The grid uses `var(--ink)` for line color. When `--ink` flips to off-white, the grid lines will become white on a black background — this works correctly without any extra overrides.

**Buttons** — If buttons use `background: var(--ink)` and `color: var(--base)`, they'll automatically flip correctly. But if any button has hardcoded `background: #0A0A08`, add an override.

**Images and SVGs** — If the template uses any `filter: invert()` images, you may need:
```css
html.dark img.invert-on-dark { filter: invert(1); }
```

**The `.spec-cell--dark` and `.feat-card--dark` components** — These already use `--ink` for their dark backgrounds, so when `--ink` flips to off-white in dark mode, they become light cards. You'll want to preserve their dark look:

```css
html.dark .spec-cell--dark,
html.dark .feat-card--dark {
    background: #1A1A18;   /* Keep them dark in dark mode */
    color: #F5F5F0;
}
```

